06:31:06,830 --> 06:31:13,320
the takeaways that you guys should have and carry into your own setups for this, this SDRs.

7330
06:31:13,320 --> 06:31:17,720
All right, so I think one of the most important things is going end-to-end.

7331
06:31:17,720 --> 06:31:21,480
And this is something I hope I showed in my demo, but that I'm really trying to push,

7332
06:31:21,480 --> 06:31:25,840
is that it's very simple to just prompt back and forth with Grokbot,

7333
06:31:25,840 --> 06:31:30,360
or to have Grokbot do a single task, like sending an email for you.

7334
06:31:30,360 --> 06:31:33,680
But I think really you should push it to do the entire workflow.

7335
06:31:33,680 --> 06:31:37,960
And it's a lot of pain up front for you to prompt back and forth, to build this system,

7336
06:31:37,960 --> 06:31:40,560
to figure out what actually makes this system work.

7337
06:31:40,560 --> 06:31:44,320
But if you stick through it and you're persistent and you train it on your style,

7338
06:31:44,320 --> 06:31:47,240
you will get so much more benefit when it's able to go end-to-end,

7339
06:31:47,240 --> 06:31:50,600
when it's able to pull people in from prospecting, it's able to enrich them,

7340
06:31:50,600 --> 06:31:54,040
it's able to understand all the context, and then it's able to push that out

7341
06:31:54,040 --> 06:31:56,720
and actually outbound them and do the full process.

7342
06:31:56,720 --> 06:31:59,480
And I think that's really what differentiates Grokbot

7343
06:31:59,480 --> 06:32:02,960
and what makes it a true force multiplier for SDRs.

7344
06:32:02,960 --> 06:32:05,920
So I really emphasize thinking at a high level

7345
06:32:05,920 --> 06:32:08,960
and kind of thinking how you can actually build that system.

7346
06:32:08,960 --> 06:32:12,640
And I think on that same note, you should be intentional here.

7347
06:32:12,640 --> 06:32:16,000
So it's really intuitive to just prompt each bot.

7348
06:32:16,000 --> 06:32:19,280
And what I highly recommend is just taking a step back and thinking,

7349
06:32:19,280 --> 06:32:22,800
OK, let me build this all through my actual chief of staff.

7350
06:32:22,800 --> 06:32:24,520
Bots should be able to talk to each other.

7351
06:32:24,520 --> 06:32:26,040
They should have that context.

7352
06:32:26,040 --> 06:32:28,440
The point of this is to offload more work from you

7353
06:32:28,440 --> 06:32:30,480
and help you actually get higher outputs.

7354
06:32:30,480 --> 06:32:33,520
And so you shouldn't actually be focusing even harder

7355
06:32:33,520 --> 06:32:34,880
and messaging even more bots.

7356
06:32:34,880 --> 06:32:37,920
It's exhausting from just all the prompt and context switching

7357
06:32:37,920 --> 06:32:39,200
you're doing there.

7358
06:32:39,200 --> 06:32:42,040
And lastly, what I kind of hope I really show in my demo

7359
06:32:42,040 --> 06:32:45,680
is how to think systematically about your setup.

7360
06:32:45,680 --> 06:32:49,520
I think it is very easy to just always want to make new bots.

7361
06:32:49,520 --> 06:32:51,680
It's kind of fun and it's kind of exciting.

7362
06:32:51,680 --> 06:32:53,640
But as someone who's built an army of bots,

7363
06:32:53,640 --> 06:32:55,800
I promise you I've had way too many at some points.

7364
06:32:55,800 --> 06:32:59,040
And it's honestly more chaotic and it does more harm than good.

7365
06:32:59,040 --> 06:33:00,880
And so you should really be questioning,

7366
06:33:00,880 --> 06:33:02,800
why is it important that a new bot does this?

7367
06:33:02,800 --> 06:33:06,800
Why can my existing email bot not just write my emails

7368
06:33:06,800 --> 06:33:09,880
